  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Train the pair auditor and benchmark on long contracts\n",
        "\n",
        "**Decided protocol**\n",
        "\n",
        "The architecture is **not** one Transformer over 20 pages. BERT/Legal-BERT max out at 256–512 tokens. A long contract is **segmented**, **structure-guided pairs** are proposed, each pair is scored, and the output is `[{span_a, span_b, type, score}]`.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Track | Job | Data |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| A. Pair classifier | Two spans in → conflict? | BCC train/dev/test **pairs** (all gold we have) |\n",
        "| B. Document reviewer | Long contract in → list of pairs | Frozen test `contract_id`s; **CUAD full text**; long table = ≥20 pages |\n",
        "\n",
        "Document metrics (same for our model and NVIDIA): word **Jaccard ≥ 0.5 on both spans**, greedy 1–1 match, micro **P / R / F1**, gold-positive **recall by gap**. Temperature **0.2** for LLMs. Do not train on NVIDIA outputs.\n",
        "\n",
        "Run from the **repo root** kernel (`PYTHONPATH=.`)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import json, os, sys\n",
        "\n",
        "ROOT = Path.cwd()\n",
        "if not (ROOT / 'auditor').exists() and (ROOT.parent / 'auditor').exists():\n",
        "    ROOT = ROOT.parent\n",
        "os.chdir(ROOT)\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n",
        "print('ROOT', ROOT.resolve())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Training data (all labeled BCC pairs we can use)\n",
        "\n",
        "Useful labeled data is **only** Better Call CLAUSE pairs (CUAD + ContractNLI perturbations). Extra EDGAR dumps without gold cannot produce F1. If `data/clause-legal` is cloned, ingest builds `artifacts/pairs.jsonl` (~140k rows)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from auditor.ingest import ingest\n",
        "\n",
        "bcc = ROOT / 'data' / 'clause-legal'\n",
        "pairs_full = ROOT / 'artifacts' / 'pairs.jsonl'\n",
        "pairs_colab = ROOT / 'artifacts' / 'pairs_colab.jsonl'\n",
        "\n",
        "if bcc.exists() and not pairs_full.exists():\n",
        "    stats = ingest(bcc, pairs_full)\n",
        "    print(json.dumps(stats, indent=2))\n",
        "elif pairs_full.exists():\n",
        "    print('using existing', pairs_full, 'bytes', pairs_full.stat().st_size)\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print('no BCC clone; will train on', pairs_colab)\n",
        "\n",
        "PAIRS = pairs_full if pairs_full.exists() else pairs_colab\n",
        "assert PAIRS.exists(), 'Need artifacts/pairs.jsonl or pairs_colab.jsonl'\n",
        "print('train file', PAIRS)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Train pair scorer (this is the trainable part of the architecture)\n",
        "\n",
        "Segmenter + candidate graph are rules (not trained). Train TF–IDF logistic on the pair table (CPU). Legal-BERT weights from Colab are attached at inference if `artifacts/legalbert-dca/` exists. Uncomment the HuggingFace loop only on GPU."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from auditor.train_baseline import train_baseline\n",
        "\n",
        "metrics = train_baseline(PAIRS, ROOT / 'artifacts', train_cap=28000)\n",
        "print('n_train', metrics['n_train'])\n",
        "print('test', {k: metrics['test'][k] for k in ('precision','recall','f1','f1_by_gap_bin_gold_positives')})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Load long-document test slice and the full pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "Prefer `llm_testset_long.jsonl` (≥20-page CUAD, frozen test ids). Fallback: full CUAD attach, then stitched slice."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from auditor.align import load_jsonl, document_prf, micro_average\n",
        "from auditor.infer import load_auditor\n",
        "\n",
        "for name in ('llm_testset_long.jsonl', 'llm_testset_full.jsonl', 'llm_testset.jsonl'):\n",
        "    p = ROOT / 'artifacts' / name\n",
        "    if p.exists():\n",
        "        DOCS = p\n",
        "        break\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    raise SystemExit('Run scripts/make_llm_testset.py and scripts/attach_full_contracts.py')\n",
        "\n",
        "docs = load_jsonl(DOCS)\n",
        "print('docs', len(docs), 'from', DOCS.name)\n",
        "print('chars', min(d['text_chars'] for d in docs), '–', max(d['text_chars'] for d in docs))\n",
        "print('gold pairs', sum(d['n_gold'] for d in docs))\n",
        "\n",
        "auditor = load_auditor(ROOT)\n",
        "print('backend', auditor.backend)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Run architecture on each long document and score vs gold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "JACCARD = 0.5\n",
        "THRESHOLD = 0.55\n",
        "per = []\n",
        "for i, doc in enumerate(docs):\n",
        "    out = auditor.analyze(doc['text'], threshold=THRESHOLD, top_k=40, max_pairs=200)\n",
        "    stats = document_prf(out['findings'], doc.get('gold') or [], threshold=JACCARD)\n",
        "    stats['contract_id'] = doc.get('contract_id')\n",
        "    per.append(stats)\n",
        "    if i < 3 or (i + 1) == len(docs):\n",
        "        print(i + 1, doc.get('contract_id', '')[:60], 'P', round(stats['precision'], 3), 'R', round(stats['recall'], 3), 'F1', round(stats['f1'], 3), 'pred', stats['n_pred'], 'gold', stats['n_gold'])\n",
        "\n",
        "ours = micro_average(per)\n",
        "ours['backend'] = auditor.backend\n",
        "print(json.dumps({k: ours[k] for k in ours if k != 'per_doc'}, indent=2))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. NVIDIA LLMs (same docs, same Jaccard)\n",
        "\n",
        "Set `NVIDIA_API_KEY`. Uses `gpt-oss-120b` by default. Skip if no key. Do not fine-tune on these outputs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from auditor.llm_nvidia import predict_pairs\n",
        "\n",
        "NVIDIA_MODEL = os.environ.get('NVIDIA_MODEL', 'openai/gpt-oss-120b')\n",
        "llm_summary = None\n",
        "if os.environ.get('NVIDIA_API_KEY') or os.environ.get('NGC_API_KEY'):\n",
        "    llm_per = []\n",
        "    for doc in docs:\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            findings = predict_pairs(doc['text'][:120000], model=NVIDIA_MODEL, temperature=0.2)\n",
        "        except Exception as e:\n",
        "            print('NVIDIA error', e)\n",
        "            findings = []\n",
        "        stats = document_prf(findings, doc.get('gold') or [], threshold=JACCARD)\n",
        "        stats['contract_id'] = doc.get('contract_id')\n",
        "        llm_per.append(stats)\n",
        "    llm_summary = micro_average(llm_per)\n",
        "    llm_summary['backend'] = NVIDIA_MODEL\n",
        "    print(json.dumps(llm_summary, indent=2))\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print('NVIDIA_API_KEY not set — auditor metrics only')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Comparison table"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "pair_m = json.loads((ROOT / 'artifacts' / 'metrics.json').read_text()) if (ROOT / 'artifacts' / 'metrics.json').exists() else {}\n",
        "lb_m = json.loads((ROOT / 'artifacts' / 'metrics_legalbert.json').read_text()) if (ROOT / 'artifacts' / 'metrics_legalbert.json').exists() else {}\n",
        "rows = [\n",
        "    {'model': 'TF–IDF pair classifier (given two spans)', 'task': 'pair', **(pair_m.get('test') or {})},\n",
        "    {'model': 'Legal-BERT pair classifier (given two spans)', 'task': 'pair',\n",
        "     'precision': lb_m.get('test_precision'), 'recall': lb_m.get('test_recall'), 'f1': lb_m.get('test_f1')},\n",
        "    {'model': f\"Auditor on long docs ({ours.get('backend')})\", 'task': 'document',\n",
        "     'precision': ours.get('precision'), 'recall': ours.get('recall'), 'f1': ours.get('f1'),\n",
        "     'n': ours.get('n_docs')},\n",
        "]\n",
        "if llm_summary:\n",
        "    rows.append({'model': llm_summary.get('backend'), 'task': 'document',\n",
        "                 'precision': llm_summary.get('precision'), 'recall': llm_summary.get('recall'), 'f1': llm_summary.get('f1')})\n",
        "\n",
        "out = {'document_eval': ours, 'nvidia': llm_summary, 'pair_tfidf': pair_m.get('test'), 'pair_legalbert': lb_m, 'docs_file': str(DOCS)}\n",
        "(ROOT / 'artifacts' / 'doc_benchmark.json').write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=2), encoding='utf-8')\n",
        "\n",
        "print('model | task | P | R | F1')\n",
        "for r in rows:\n",
        "    p, rec, f1 = r.get('precision'), r.get('recall'), r.get('f1')\n",
        "    def fmt(x):\n",
        "        return f'{x:.3f}' if isinstance(x, (int, float)) else '—'\n",
        "    print(r.get('model'), '|', r.get('task'), '|', fmt(p), '|', fmt(rec), '|', fmt(f1))\n",
      ]
    }
  ]
}
